{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Only the trees of which you know that they are not trees for food, them you shall destroy and cut down.</b> To make a siege-work from them. And in the first chapter of Ta'anit it concludes: What is meant by כי האדם עץ השדה — is a human then a tree of the field? Rather, the verse speaks of a Torah scholar — that is, if he is a fitting Torah scholar, from him you shall eat and him you shall not cut down; but if not, him you shall destroy and cut down, and do not study before him. And if it is a student who is unfit, do not leave him before you."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:01:07.795026559Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}